    "result_text": "The build is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Change made:**\n- Added a small, single-responsibility component `OwnerAuditor` (`src/main/java/.../service/OwnerAuditor.java`) that logs to the dedicated logger named `AUDIT`. Its `auditCreated(Owner)` method emits one line carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n- Wired it into `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` \u2014 the sole create entry point \u2014 invoking `ownerAuditor.auditCreated(owner)` right after `saveOwner` succeeds (at which point the id and generated `customerCode` are populated).\n\n**Why this placement:** the audit is a distinct side-effect concern, so it lives in its own class rather than being bolted onto `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` (which is shared by the update path) or the controller inline. Emitting after the save, on the successful-create branch only, guarantees the values logged exactly match what a subsequent `GET` returns.\n\nThe audit line format is `owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-17`, and the acceptance test's `anyContains` check (id, customerCode, registrationDate all present) passes. Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
